        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Not a mockup: these spreads are rendered from the production PDF. Photographs
      of the printed copy replace them the day it arrives.</p>
      <table class="spec">
        <tr><td>Trim</td><td>6 × 9 in</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Binding</td><td>Perfect bound paperback, on every edition. Volumes are capped near
        300 pages; a longer archive becomes a quarterly set of thinner volumes rather than one
        oversized book.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Paper</td><td>60# uncoated white, black ink</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cover</td><td>Matte, in the classic literary style: ivory ground, red and black rules, your masthead set in type</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Length</td><td>32&ndash;300 pages per volume; longer archives become a quarterly set</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Apparatus</td><td>Contents with page numbers, running headers, article notes and bylines per article</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Price</td><td>The service is free for authors during the beta. Readers pay the
        printer; you choose whether the list price carries a margin, and beta editions default
        to exact cost. Measured on a real order: a 294-page edition landed for $16.58 including
